// SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
//
// What every Forms sample carries inside its executable.
//
// A resource script is compiled by the build and folded into the binary, so
// everything below travels in the .exe rather than beside it:
//
//     stainless build demo.sl forms.rc ...
//
// `llvm-rc` resolves an #include, and a file named by a relative path, against
// this script's own directory -- so `forms.manifest` is found whichever
// directory the build was started from.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- manifest
//
// 24 is RT_MANIFEST and 1 is CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID, which is the
// name the loader looks under for an executable's own manifest. This is read
// before any code in the program runs, which is why nothing asks for it.
//
// It is what selects version 6 of comctl32. Without it Windows loads version 5
// and the tabs, toolbar and progress bar come out looking like Windows 2000 --
// they work either way, which is what makes the omission easy to miss.
1 24 "forms.manifest"

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ strings
//
// A string table, to show the mechanism: `Resources.Text(id)` reads one back.
// Strings are stored in blocks of sixteen, so ids that sit together cost one
// block rather than one each.
STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    1000 "Stainless Forms"
    1001 "Built with resources compiled into the binary"
END
